.TH PATH_LEN 3
.SH NAME
path_len \- compute the length of a path component
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include <path.h>
.PP
.BI "size_t path_len(const char* " s ", size_t " n ");"
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B path_len
calculates the length in bytes of the first path component within the string
.I s
of length
.IR n .
.PP
The function scans the provided buffer and stops upon encountering the first path separator character or reaching the end of the specified length
.IR n .
It correctly handles multi-byte UTF-8 sequences, ensuring that path separator detection only triggers on single-byte characters.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns the number of bytes from the start of the input string to the first path separator character or the end of the string.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR path_skip_component (3),
.BR path_skip (3)